  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "WEIGHTED DEPENDENCY GRAPHS AND THE ISING MODEL — Weighted dependency graphs have been recently introduced by the second author, as a toolbox to prove central limit theorems.\n\n**WEIGHTED DEPENDENCY GRAPHS AND THE ISING MODEL**\n\n*JEHANNE DOUSSE AND VALENTIN FÉRAY*\n\n24 pp, 20 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** Weighted dependency graphs have been recently introduced by the second author, as a toolbox to prove central limit theorems. In this paper, we prove that spins in the d-dimensional Ising model display such a weighted dependency structure. We use this to obtain various central limit theorems for the number of occurrences of local and global patterns in a growing box.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction and statement of results; 1.1 Cumulants in the Ising model; 1.2 Weighted dependency graphs; 1.3 Central limit theorems; 2.1 The Ising model; 1.4 Outline of the paper; 2 Preliminaries; 2.2 Joint cumulants; 2.3 Spanning trees of maximal weight and tree ; 2.4 Weighted dependency graphs; 3 Cluster expansions and bounds on joint cumul; 3.1 At very high temperature, without magnetic; 3.2 At very low temperature, without magnetic ; 4.1 Weighted dependency graph for the i's and ; 3.3 With a strong magnetic field; 4 Weighted dependency graphs and central limit; 4.2 Central limit theorem for occurrences of g",
      "lang": "en",
